        "why": "Expected Loss is the statistical mean loss expected over a horizon, which banks cover via P&L provisions and loan pricing. Unexpected Loss represents the dispersion or tail risk around the mean, requiring Common Equity Tier 1 and Tier 2 capital buffers to ensure institutional solvency."
