        "answer": 0,
        "answerIndex": 0,
        "why": "Funded Credit-Linked Notes (CLNs) eliminate counterparty credit risk because the cash proceeds are held in segregated, bankruptcy-remote high-quality collateral, allowing the bank to immediately write down note principal when losses occur."
